LOCUS       hostile                  240 bp    DNA     circular SYN 27-JUL-2026
DEFINITION  Feature names that break a naive PostScript or PDF string writer.
COMMENT     Every name here is hostile to a specific escaping bug, and the first
            one is real: aph(3')-Ia is the gene this project's own feature
            database calls KanR. An unescaped ')' ends a PostScript string
            literal and turns the rest of the program into garbage, so the whole
            figure is lost to one gene name. Without a fixture containing one,
            the check for it cannot fail and therefore proves nothing.
FEATURES             Location/Qualifiers
     source          1..240
                     /organism="synthetic DNA construct"
                     /mol_type="other DNA"
     CDS             1..60
                     /label="aph(3')-Ia"
     CDS             61..120
                     /label="back\slash"
     CDS             121..180
                     /label="paren (unclosed"
     CDS             181..240
                     /label="Olschlager 1989"
ORIGIN
        1 atgagccata ttcaacggga aacgtcttgc tcgaggccgc gattaaattc caacatggat
       61 gctgatttat atgggtataa atgggctcgc gataatgtcg ggcaatcagg tgcgacaatc
      121 tatcgattgt atgggaagcc cgatgcgcca gagttgtttc tgaaacatgg caaaggtagc
      181 gttgccaatg atgttacaga tgagatggtc agactaaact ggctgacgga atttatgcct
//
